<title>USA: Tower Automotive net up as revenues soar.</title>
<headline>Tower Automotive net up as revenues soar.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tower Automotive on Monday cited acquisitions in 1996 for helping revenues and net income double in the fourth quarter ended December 31.</p>
<p>The company said revenues in the period reached $120 million, up from $58 million one year ago, while net income totaled $6.9 million, about double the $3.5 million reported last year.</p>
<p>Tower Automotive said its purchases of MSTI and Trylon last year added significantly to its revenue stream.</p>
<p>Tower Automotive makes structural components for the automotive industry.</p>
<p>Its shares were trading up 3/8 Monday at 45-1/8.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
